# 🚀 NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR) - Reference Datasets

This repository integrates theoretical biological parameters and scientific rationale derived from open-access datasets curated by the NASA Open Science Data Repository (OSDR).

---

## 📂 Referenced Datasets

### 1. NASA OSDR OSD-514
* **Title:** Artificial gravity partially protects space-induced neurological deficits in Drosophila melanogaster
* **Platform:** Multi-use Variable-g Platform (MVP-Fly-01) aboard the International Space Station (ISS)
* **Assay Types:** RNA Sequencing (RNA-Seq), Protein Expression Profiling (Mass Spectrometry)
* **Key Findings Used:** Used as a conceptual model for spaceflight-induced neurological stress, glial phenotypes, and central nervous system (CNS) adaptation pathways under altered gravity.
* **Official URL:** [https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-514/](https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-514/)

### 2. NASA OSDR OSD-611 / OSD-612
* **Title:** Bulk RNA sequencing and single nuclei transcriptomics and epigenomics of brain tissue from spaceflight missions
* **Organism:** Mus musculus (Mouse Brain Tissue)
* **Assay Types:** Single-cell RNA Sequencing, Epigenomics
* **Key Findings Used:** Serves as the theoretical reference for space radiation stress on neuroinflammation, BDNF regulation, and cellular DNA repair pathway response.
* **Official URL:** [https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-612](https://osdr.nasa.gov/bio/repo/data/studies/OSD-612)

---

## 🔬 Data Utilization Statement
The datasets above are cited as the primary academic and empirical foundation for **AstroHelix**. Data parameters within the prototype simulation represent conceptual modeling values derived from these studies.
